{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Create a new Go module `github.com/hyperledger/fabric/sdkutils` in the Fabric repository to host all externalized utilities.",
    "The common module will be versioned alongside Fabric releases (same version as Fabric).",
    "The Fabric Go SDK will add a dependency on `github.com/hyperledger/fabric/sdkutils` and remove all copied code.",
    "For U6, the temporary workaround will be implemented in the chaincode packaging code (likely in `core/chaincode/platforms/golang`).",
    "The workaround for U6 will be marked as temporary with a clear removal timeline.",
    "All externalized packages will maintain backward compatibility with existing SDK usage patterns."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The Fabric Go SDK is using Go modules and can depend on the new module.",
    "The copied code in the SDK is mostly compatible with the Fabric codebase, and any modifications are minimal and can be merged into the common module.",
    "The development team has access to both repositories and can make coordinated changes.",
    "The common module will be published to a module proxy (e.g., proxy.golang.org) or the SDK can use a replace directive during development.",
    "The effort estimates assume a developer familiar with both codebases.",
    "The temporary workaround (U6) is only for the Go chaincode platform.",
    "The externalized code will be placed in the Fabric repository under a new directory (e.g., `sdkutils`).",
    "The existing tests in the SDK will be updated to use the new module and will pass without major changes.",
    "Integration testing will be done using the existing Fabric test network."
  ],
